From 0ccc6a75400c9decd52b05f1c7c3a4c9d6b10d40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:47:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] android, ipa: simple: light full resolution stills with
 the flash strobe

The flash lit stills with the torch (150 mA on the SM5703), from the AE
precapture to the capture. A still in the separate full resolution
configuration is now lit by the strobe (1200 mA), fired as the sensor
starts, with the exposure scaled by pre-flash metering:

- The soft IPA publishes, per frame, the light relative to what the AGC
  settles on as Lux: the mean of the linear histogram above the black
  level, over the mean the AGC last settled on, per unit of exposure time
  and gain. Unlike the exposure alone it still measures with the
  exposure at its limit, as in the dim scenes where a flash is used.
- The HAL keeps the light without the torch and with it at the end of
  the precapture. The strobe adds flash_gain (camera_hal.yaml, how much
  more light it gives than the torch) times what the torch added; the
  still starts with the exposure that gives the settled brightness.
- IPASoftInterface::start() takes the controls Camera::start() is given
  and returns sensor controls: an ExposureValue scales the exposure the
  configuration starts with, written to the sensor before streaming. The
  simple pipeline starts the software ISP before streamon for that. The
  generated proxy is regenerated from soft.mojom; the template's thread
  proxy passes the inputs of start() only, fixed by hand.
- That configuration does not update the exposure remembered for the
  sensor mode, and the AGC takes it as its last request.
- The strobe stops once the still is in; without a strobe (no
  flash_gain, or failing) the torch lights it as before.
- The JPEG's EXIF says whether the flash fired and in which mode.

